<title>SPAIN: Spain's Telefonica studies $500 mln bond issue.</title>
<headline>Spain's Telefonica studies $500 mln bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish telecoms operator Telefonica said on Tuesday it was studying a bond issue, convertible to shares, for a total $500 million, a spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue forms part of the financing programme that we have at the moment,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>&quot;The Annual Shareholders Meeting has already approved the possible issue of convertible bonds.&quot;</p>
<p>He said Morgan Stanley and UBS were assessing the issue, but did not say whether they would be the lead managers.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
